2026-08-18T15:15:22.8770874Z 
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8770949Z > 
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8771246Z > # Phase 18 is the package's exhaustive simulation/reporting harness, and the
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8772063Z > # structured-conversion contract is a generated 22,000-assertion audit. Keep
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8772888Z > # both in repository CI, but do not rerun them during routine CRAN checks.
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8773442Z > #
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8774287Z > # The second group is a CRAN check-time budget. Measured on 2026-08-10 (receipts
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8775185Z > # in docs/dev-log/release/0.7.0-cran-gate/test-timings.csv): the CRAN lane ran
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8776033Z > # 1160 s locally and 29-30 min of `checking tests` on win-builder, far above
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8776849Z > # CRAN's ~10-minute incoming guidance. Seventeen files carried 747 s of that
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8777956Z > # 1160 s; excluding them leaves 413 s locally (~6.9 min), projecting to ~10 min
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8778727Z > # on Windows at the measured 1.50x local->win-builder factor.
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8779279Z > #
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8779924Z > # These are statistical-validation suites -- bivariate association sandwiches,
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8780797Z > # the G4/G5 missing-response foundation, zero-one-beta, bivariate Gaussian, and
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8781999Z > # the profile-target matrix -- not "does the package install and work" tests.
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8782954Z > # They still run in full in repository CI, where NOT_CRAN=true. Nothing is
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8783828Z > # deleted and no test is weakened; this only changes which lane runs them.
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8784489Z > #
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8785034Z > # The patterns are ANCHORED on purpose. An unanchored "zero-one-beta" also
2026-08-18T15:15:22.8785655Z > # matches test-missing-predictor-zero-one-beta.R, and an unanchored
