2026-08-18T15:15:23.3122040Z > 
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3122239Z > # Phase 18 is the package's exhaustive simulation/reporting harness, and the
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3122444Z > # structured-conversion contract is a generated 22,000-assertion audit. Keep
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3122628Z > # both in repository CI, but do not rerun them during routine CRAN checks.
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3122697Z > #
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3122897Z > # The second group is a CRAN check-time budget. Measured on 2026-08-10 (receipts
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3123108Z > # in docs/dev-log/release/0.7.0-cran-gate/test-timings.csv): the CRAN lane ran
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3123284Z > # 1160 s locally and 29-30 min of `checking tests` on win-builder, far above
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3123469Z > # CRAN's ~10-minute incoming guidance. Seventeen files carried 747 s of that
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3123659Z > # 1160 s; excluding them leaves 413 s locally (~6.9 min), projecting to ~10 min
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3123811Z > # on Windows at the measured 1.50x local->win-builder factor.
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3123882Z > #
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3124092Z > # These are statistical-validation suites -- bivariate association sandwiches,
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3124295Z > # the G4/G5 missing-response foundation, zero-one-beta, bivariate Gaussian, and
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3124495Z > # the profile-target matrix -- not "does the package install and work" tests.
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3124677Z > # They still run in full in repository CI, where NOT_CRAN=true. Nothing is
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3124979Z > # deleted and no test is weakened; this only changes which lane runs them.
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3125048Z > #
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3125236Z > # The patterns are ANCHORED on purpose. An unanchored "zero-one-beta" also
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3125422Z > # matches test-missing-predictor-zero-one-beta.R, and an unanchored
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3125645Z > # "biv-gaussian" also matches test-missing-response-biv-gaussian.R -- neither is
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3125888Z > # intended, and both must keep running on the CRAN lane.
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3125958Z > #
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3126173Z > # `^julia` excludes every test-julia-*.R file. That alone is NOT enough: CRAN-lane
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3126363Z > # files such as test-binomial-response.R still call engine = "julia" inside
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3126562Z > # expect_error(), and Workflow G now admits fixed-effect binomial into the Julia
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3126751Z > # bridge, so the call reaches JuliaCall::julia_setup() before any rejection.
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3126940Z > # Ligges win-builder (2026-08-16/17) hung there for ~10448s even after #1061.
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3127121Z > # Defense in depth: (1) this filter, (2) drm_skip_live_julia() in live tests,
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3127324Z > # (3) drm_julia_setup() hard-blocks the CRAN lane unless DRMTMB_JULIA_TESTS=true.
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3127440Z > # The full suite still runs when NOT_CRAN=true.
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3127600Z > not_cran <- isTRUE(as.logical(Sys.getenv("NOT_CRAN", "false")))
2026-08-18T15:15:23.3127681Z > if (not_cran) {
